# ©AngelaMos | 2026
# .dockerignore.example
#
# Annotated .dockerignore template for Cybersecurity-Projects.
# Copy next to the build CONTEXT root (the path compose passes as `context:`),
# rename to `.dockerignore`.
#
# Everything not excluded here is shipped to the builder as build context.
# Three things go wrong without it:
#   1. Secrets (.env, keys) land in a layer, and `docker history` or a pushed
#      image leaks them forever.
#   2. Host node_modules/.venv (wrong libc, wrong arch) override the
#      container's own install.
#   3. Any edit to an unrelated file (docs, .git) busts the layer cache.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore-like, matched from the context root. `**` crosses
# directories, `!` re-includes, and the LAST matching line wins.
#
# Per-Dockerfile ignore files: BuildKit reads `<name>.dockerignore` next to
# the Dockerfile before falling back to this file. Use that when one context
# feeds several Dockerfiles (prod.Dockerfile.dockerignore, etc.).
#
# Docs: https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#dockerignore-files


# ── Allowlist Alternative (strongest option) ──────────────────────────────────
# Deny everything, then re-include only what the Dockerfile COPYs. A new
# secret file can never leak because nothing is shipped by default. Costs one
# line per new top-level path. To use it, delete every section below and
# uncomment this block, adjusting paths to your layout:
#
# *
# !src/
# !pyproject.toml
# !uv.lock
# !README.md
# !LICENSE
# **/__pycache__/
# **/*.py[cod]


# ── Secrets & Environment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER bake secrets into an image. Inject at runtime (env_file, secrets:).
# `**/` catches nested copies like backend/.env.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/.npmrc.local
**/.netrc
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*


# ── Version Control ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .git alone can be hundreds of MB, and it changes on every commit, which
# invalidates any `COPY . .` layer.

.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules


# ── Dependencies Installed On The Host ────────────────────────────────────────
# The image installs its own. Host copies are the wrong platform and shadow
# the container's install.

**/node_modules/
**/.pnpm-store/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
/target/
**/.zig-cache/
**/zig-out/


# ── Python Caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.ty_cache/


# ── Frontend Build Caches ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

**/dist/
/build/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage/


# ── Coverage & Reports ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage.xml
**/coverage.out


# ── Tests ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kept IN the context on purpose. Projects here run their suites inside a
# container (a `test` stage or `docker compose run`), and multi-stage builds
# only copy what each stage asks for, so tests never reach the runtime image
# anyway. Uncomment only if no stage ever runs tests.
#
# tests/
# **/conftest.py


# ── Container Definitions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Changing a compose file should not rebuild the image.

**/Dockerfile*
**/*.Dockerfile
**/*.dockerfile
**/*.docker
**/compose*.yml
**/compose*.yaml
**/*.compose.yml
**/docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore


# ── Documentation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# README.md and LICENSE are RE-INCLUDED: pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, and the build backend aborts without it, so a
# `uv sync` that installs the project inside the image fails.

docs/
learn/
**/*.md
!README.md
!LICENSE
**/*.rst


# ── Dev Tooling & CI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.github/
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.editorconfig
.style.yapf
justfile
Makefile
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed/
.claude/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo


# ── Logs, Local Databases, OS Junk ────────────────────────────────────────────

**/*.log
**/logs/
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/dump.rdb
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
